# Line-ending policy (#246).
#
# The tunnel contract fixtures are shared with base-studio-code and their own `$comment`
# claims they are BYTE-IDENTICAL to the desktop copy. On a Windows checkout without this
# file that claim is false in the working tree — Git stores LF but checks out CRLF, so
# mobile's copy measured 5474 bytes against the desktop's 5376 (98 CRLFs) and any
# working-tree hash comparison false-fails.
#
# Pinning eol=lf repo-wide fixes the working tree without touching a single blob (Git
# already normalizes to LF on the way in), and makes the byte-identical claim literally
# true for anyone who checks.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The contract fixtures specifically — stated explicitly so the rule survives any future
# narrowing of the wildcard above.
*.fixtures.json text eol=lf
